# {{ .Name }} ({{ .Type | title }})

Provides a SAML authentication domain resource. It depends on a `wallix-bastion_externalauth_saml`
resource for the actual identity provider configuration.

## Example Usage

```terraform
resource "wallix-bastion_externalauth_saml" "corporate" {
  authentication_name = "corporate_saml"
  idp_metadata        = file("${path.module}/idp-metadata.xml")
  timeout             = 30

  claim_customization {
    username    = "username"
    displayname = "displayname"
    email       = "email"
    group       = "group"
  }
}

resource "wallix-bastion_authdomain_saml" "corporate" {
  domain_name          = "corporate.saml"
  auth_domain_name     = "corporate.com"
  external_auths       = [wallix-bastion_externalauth_saml.corporate.authentication_name]
  default_email_domain = "corporate.com"
  default_language     = "en"
  label                = "Corporate SAML"
  description          = "Corporate SAML authentication domain"
}
```

{{ .SchemaMarkdown | trimspace }}

## Usage Notes

### Relationship to externalauth_saml

`external_auths` references one or more `wallix-bastion_externalauth_saml.authentication_name`
values, which define the actual SAML identity provider connection. This resource layers Bastion's
authentication-domain concept (default language, default email domain, label) on top of it.

### default_language

Must be one of `de`, `en`, `es`, `fr`, `ru`.

### idp_initiated_url

Computed attribute exposing the URL used for identity-provider-initiated SSO.

## Import

SAML authentication domain can be imported using the domain name, e.g.

```shell
terraform import wallix-bastion_authdomain_saml.corporate corporate.saml
```
